{
  "_comment": [
    "Example MCP wiring for the optional knowledge runtime. Copy to .mcp.json",
    "(gitignored) and adjust the interpreter path for your environment.",
    "",
    "'command' must be the interpreter that has agentic_vault_knowledge",
    "installed. If you installed into a venv at the vault root, that is",
    ".venv/bin/python (macOS/Linux) or .venv/Scripts/python.exe (Windows);",
    "a bare 'python' only works if the runtime is on the default interpreter.",
    "",
    "The launcher resolves the vault root from its own location, so no absolute",
    "path is needed here and the same entry works on any machine that clones",
    "the vault. ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-.} is Claude Code's project root; the",
    ":-. default is required because CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR is set in the server's",
    "environment, not the client's, so a bare ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR} is empty.",
    "Other clients: substitute their project-root variable, or use an absolute",
    "path — only this file needs to know it.",
    "",
    "Writes are OFF by default. To allow knowledge_apply_patch/apply_batch to",
    "mutate canonical Markdown, add:",
    "  \"env\": { \"AGENTIC_VAULT_KNOWLEDGE_READ_ONLY\": \"0\" }"
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "vault-knowledge": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-.}/.venv/Scripts/python.exe",
      "args": [
        "${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-.}/.agent/scripts/vault-knowledge-mcp.py"
      ]
    }
  }
}
